Refuse approval attempts from untrusted channels out loud

Approval commands were only parsed on trusted channels, so an attacker emailing
"approve 1" fell through to the planner and got answered like ordinary
conversation. Nothing unsafe executed, but the refusal was invisible and left
no audit record of the attempt.

Approval commands are now recognised on every channel and refused by
approvals.resolve() when the channel is not trusted, which produces both an
explicit reply and an approval_refused_untrusted audit entry.

Verified live: attacker emails "approve 1" against a held action and receives
"email is not a trusted channel", with the attempt recorded.

Also adds scripts/send_email.py for driving arbitrary inbound email, a
regression check for this path (selftest now 24 checks), and a rewritten
demo script with the screen layout.

